The thick section of the graph below is the piece of $y=\tan x$ kept when the domain is restricted.
State the interval, using correct bracket notation.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, xmin=-5.4, xmax=5.4, ymin=-5.8, ymax=4.4, samples=150, clip=false, width=11cm, height=8cm, xtick={-4.7124,-1.5708,1.5708,4.7124}, xticklabels={$-\frac{3\pi}{2}$,$-\frac{\pi}{2}$,$\frac{\pi}{2}$,$\frac{3\pi}{2}$}, every tick label/.style={font=\scriptsize}]
\addplot[thick, <->, domain=-4.479:-1.804] {tan(deg(x))};
\addplot[very thick, red, <->, domain=-1.3374:1.3374] {tan(deg(x))};
\addplot[thick, <->, domain=1.804:4.479] {tan(deg(x))};
\addplot[dashed, domain=-4.2:4.2] ({-1.5708},{x});
\addplot[dashed, domain=-4.2:4.2] ({1.5708},{x});
\addplot[dashed, domain=-4.2:4.2] ({-4.7124},{x});
\addplot[dashed, domain=-4.2:4.2] ({4.7124},{x});
